{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791147440,"nonce":"5rD4xIAeuYiw4db1LcjFvJtCVq8=","title":"Rich text editor: a block's text wraps inside its own one-line box and overlaps what follows","message":"Every heading in rich_text_editor_demo wrapped across two lines while\nits container stayed one line tall, so the second line drew over the\nparagraph below. Inline code tokens broke mid-word the same way\n(\"RichDocumen\" / \"t\").\n\nPRE-EXISTING, not caused by the recent text work. Confirmed by building\nthe demo at c6531f4a, before the variable-weight, CSS line-height and\nsystem-ui commits: identical breakage, same headings, same overlaps.\n\n\nrich_text_editor/render.rs sizes each visual line's CONTAINER, with\ndiv().w(line_width).h(line_height_px), but leaves the text child\ncontent-sized. taffy then hands the child min-content, so it wraps at\nthe longest word regardless of the container's width, inside a box that\nis already exactly one line tall.\n\nThe editor's own wrapper was right all along. Instrumented, it measures\n\"The Rich Text Editor\" at 289.5px against a 720px limit and correctly\ndecides one visual line. The wrap came from the child's own layout,\nafter that decision.\n\n\nThe single-run path now passes the width to the child as well as the\ncontainer. Headings, lists and the block quote all render correctly.\n\n\nA line with several runs, which is how inline code is built, positions\neach run absolutely at a precomputed x and leaves both the positioned\nbox and its child content-sized, so those runs still wrap mid-token.\n\nSizing them to the run's measured width fixes the wrap but removes the\nspacing between runs: the text comes out \"a RichDocument via\" with the\nspaces gone, because a run's measured width excludes the space that\nseparates it from the next. So the width and the inter-run advance\ndisagree about who owns the space, and that has to be settled before\nthis path can be sized. Not committed; one visual defect traded for\nanother is not a fix.","files":null}]}